From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:02:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] i386-asm: assembler forms of the 32-bit kernel, musl and
 busybox

Found by building the 32-bit kernel, musl and busybox for i386:

- clobbers: "rax", "rcx", "rdx" are the 32-bit registers in 32-bit code
  (the kernel's shared x86 headers), a leading '%' is skipped ("%eax",
  busybox);
- mov between a segment register and memory infers a 16-bit move
  ("mov PT_FS(%esp), %fs"), and the store form never gets the 0x66
  prefix, like GNU as;
- a segment register name as a statement is its prefix byte
  ("ds;ds;ds;int $0x80" in the vDSO's ALTERNATIVE), alone or before an
  instruction;
- ".previous" after a ".text" with no ".section" yet returns to .text;
- ud2a, sysenter, sysexit; rdpid and invpcid with a 32-bit register;
- "call *%gs:16" (musl's system call): the '*' survives the re-parse of
  the operand after the segment prefix (it became a direct call);
- the x87 constraints "t"/"u" on i386 (musl's math: "fabs" : "+t"(x)),
  as asm registers 8 and 9 mapped to TREG_ST0, for any floating type;
- an "m" input operand with no register left for its address is copied
  to a stack temporary (busybox's comba multiply: three register outputs,
  two clobbers, two pointer-based memory inputs);
- tcc's own linker applies R_386_8/PC8 and R_386_16/PC16 for any output
  format ("jecxz 1f" in musl's sigsetjmp.s).

Fixes 76, 77, 79, 80, 81, 90, 91, 92 and 93 of the tinycc-os-kernel
project (docs/FIX-LOG.md).
---
 i386-asm.c   | 132 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 i386-gen.c   |   2 +-
 i386-link.c  |  35 ++++++++++----
 tccasm.c     |   5 +-
 x86_64-asm.h |   6 +++
 5 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

